<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:id="@+id/widget_root"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:padding="4dp"
    android:background="@drawable/widget_outer_bg">

    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/widget_battery_card"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="0dp"
        android:layout_weight="3"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:padding="7dp"
        android:background="@drawable/widget_card_bg"
        android:gravity="center_vertical">

        <!--
          BUD COLUMN — two bud drawables, side by side with a GAP between them.

          Both buds are the same 62 x 96dp drawable (ratio 0.641) that the app card
          uses, so the widget shows the same artwork, just smaller.

          THE BOX RATIO MUST MATCH THE ART RATIO (fixed 2026-09-18). Two bugs came
          from getting this wrong, and both were visible in the layout report:

          1. SQUISHED (first report): the row was `wrap_content` with a fixed 34dp
             bud width, so the width was the binding constraint in `fitCenter` — the
             ink drew 34dp wide and ~53dp tall in a ~74dp slot, leaving dead space
             above and below.

          2. FAT ON THE VERTICAL AXIS (second report): raising the box to 72dp made
             it WIDER than the art ratio needs, so `fitCenter` scaled the ink UP in
             width to fill the box — 72dp wide against 96dp of ink height, a rendered
             ratio of 0.75 instead of the true 0.641. Nothing was distorted in the
             file; the box was simply the wrong SHAPE and the art stretched to it.

          `fitCenter` scales to whichever bound is proportionally SMALLER, so the
          only way to keep the true ratio at every widget size is for the BOX to
          carry the true ratio itself: width/height = 0.641. That is what
          `widget_bud_width` and `widget_bud_height` now are — a matched pair, 72 x
          112dp (72 / 0.641 = 112). The row keeps `match_parent` height, so the ink
          scales down cleanly on small widgets and up on large ones, always at 0.641.

          DO NOT change one of these dimens without changing the other, and keep the
          ratio 0.641 (the source viewBox is 460 x 717.456). The in-app battery card
          solves the same problem identically with battery_bud_width/battery_wear_height
          (62 x 96dp, same 0.641) — match that pattern, not a stretched slot.
        -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/widget_bud_row"
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="match_parent"
            android:orientation="horizontal"
            android:gravity="center_vertical"
            android:paddingTop="2dp"
            android:paddingBottom="2dp">

            <ImageView
                android:id="@+id/widget_bud_left"
                android:layout_width="@dimen/widget_bud_width"
                android:layout_height="@dimen/widget_bud_height"
                android:scaleType="fitCenter"
                android:src="@drawable/ic_bud_left"
                android:contentDescription="@string/widget_battery_left" />

            <!--
              The gap between the buds.

              THIS IS A TextView, NOT A View, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE (2026-09-18).
              It was a bare <View> with a fixed width. RemoteViews supports a limited
              view set and builds its layout on the LAUNCHER's process from a
              whitelist: a plain View is NOT reliably instantiated there. The
              inflation succeeds in-process (which is why every layout report looked
              perfect and buildViews() never threw) but the launcher fails to build
              the view tree from the parcel, and shows "Can't load widget" — an error
              that comes from the HOST, which is why nothing in this app ever saw it.

              That is the exact shape of this bug: measurements fine, parcel fine,
              logic fine, and the widget still refused. A TextView with no text is
              inert, is on the whitelist, and is the standard spacer in widget
              layouts.
            -->
            <TextView
                android:layout_width="@dimen/widget_bud_gap"
                android:layout_height="1dp" />

            <ImageView
                android:id="@+id/widget_bud_right"
                android:layout_width="@dimen/widget_bud_width"
                android:layout_height="@dimen/widget_bud_height"
                android:scaleType="fitCenter"
                android:src="@drawable/ic_bud_right"
                android:contentDescription="@string/widget_battery_right" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:paddingStart="10dp">

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/widget_row_left"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:layout_marginBottom="4dp">

                <TextView
                    android:layout_width="14dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/widget_battery_left"
                    android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
                    android:textSize="11sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold" />

                <ProgressBar
                    android:id="@+id/widget_bar_left"
                    style="@android:style/Widget.ProgressBar.Horizontal"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="5dp"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:layout_marginStart="8dp"
                    android:layout_marginEnd="6dp"
                    android:max="100"
                    android:progress="0"
                    android:progressDrawable="@drawable/widget_battery_bar" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/widget_text_left"
                    android:layout_width="28dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text=""
                    android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
                    android:textSize="10sp"
                    android:gravity="end" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/widget_row_case"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:layout_marginBottom="4dp">

                <TextView
                    android:layout_width="14dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/widget_battery_case"
                    android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
                    android:textSize="11sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold" />

                <ProgressBar
                    android:id="@+id/widget_bar_case"
                    style="@android:style/Widget.ProgressBar.Horizontal"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="5dp"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:layout_marginStart="8dp"
                    android:layout_marginEnd="6dp"
                    android:max="100"
                    android:progress="0"
                    android:progressDrawable="@drawable/widget_battery_bar" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/widget_text_case"
                    android:layout_width="28dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text=""
                    android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
                    android:textSize="10sp"
                    android:gravity="end" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/widget_row_right"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:gravity="center_vertical">

                <TextView
                    android:layout_width="14dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/widget_battery_right"
                    android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
                    android:textSize="11sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold" />

                <ProgressBar
                    android:id="@+id/widget_bar_right"
                    style="@android:style/Widget.ProgressBar.Horizontal"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="5dp"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:layout_marginStart="8dp"
                    android:layout_marginEnd="6dp"
                    android:max="100"
                    android:progress="0"
                    android:progressDrawable="@drawable/widget_battery_bar" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/widget_text_right"
                    android:layout_width="28dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text=""
                    android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
                    android:textSize="10sp"
                    android:gravity="end" />
            </LinearLayout>
        </LinearLayout>
    </LinearLayout>

    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/widget_anc_segments"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="0dp"
        android:layout_weight="1"
        android:layout_marginTop="4dp"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:padding="2dp"
        android:background="@drawable/widget_segment_container">

        <TextView android:id="@+id/widget_seg_off"
            android:layout_width="0dp" android:layout_height="match_parent"
            android:layout_weight="1" android:gravity="center"
            android:text="@string/widget_anc_off"
            android:textColor="@color/widget_segment_text"
            android:textSize="10sp" android:textStyle="bold"
            android:background="@drawable/widget_segment_bg" />

        <TextView android:id="@+id/widget_seg_trans"
            android:layout_width="0dp" android:layout_height="match_parent"
            android:layout_weight="1" android:gravity="center"
            android:text="@string/widget_anc_trans"
            android:textColor="@color/widget_segment_text"
            android:textSize="10sp" android:textStyle="bold"
            android:background="@drawable/widget_segment_bg" />

        <TextView android:id="@+id/widget_seg_low"
            android:layout_width="0dp" android:layout_height="match_parent"
            android:layout_weight="1" android:gravity="center"
            android:text="@string/widget_anc_low"
            android:textColor="@color/widget_segment_text"
            android:textSize="10sp" android:textStyle="bold"
            android:background="@drawable/widget_segment_bg" />

        <TextView android:id="@+id/widget_seg_med"
            android:layout_width="0dp" android:layout_height="match_parent"
            android:layout_weight="1" android:gravity="center"
            android:text="@string/widget_anc_med"
            android:textColor="@color/widget_segment_text"
            android:textSize="10sp" android:textStyle="bold"
            android:background="@drawable/widget_segment_bg" />

        <TextView android:id="@+id/widget_seg_high"
            android:layout_width="0dp" android:layout_height="match_parent"
            android:layout_weight="1" android:gravity="center"
            android:text="@string/widget_anc_high"
            android:textColor="@color/widget_segment_text"
            android:textSize="10sp" android:textStyle="bold"
            android:background="@drawable/widget_segment_bg" />
    </LinearLayout>

    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/widget_game_row"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="0dp"
        android:layout_weight="1"
        android:layout_marginTop="4dp"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:paddingStart="8dp"
        android:paddingEnd="8dp"
        android:background="@drawable/widget_card_bg"
        android:gravity="center_vertical">

        <TextView
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:text="@string/widget_game_mode_label"
            android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
            android:textSize="12sp" />

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/widget_game_switch"
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:minWidth="52dp"
            android:paddingStart="14dp"
            android:paddingEnd="14dp"
            android:paddingTop="4dp"
            android:paddingBottom="4dp"
            android:gravity="center"
            android:text="OFF"
            android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
            android:textSize="11sp"
            android:textStyle="bold"
            android:background="@drawable/widget_button_bg" />
    </LinearLayout>

    <!--
      CONNECTION STATUS, shown in the widget's empty state.

      WHY THIS EXISTS: disconnected, every battery row is gated INVISIBLE (no data),
      so the widget rendered as a blank card — indistinguishable from a broken one,
      and reported as "the widget won't load". It was loading; it had nothing to say.
      The widget now says so explicitly, using the same dot-and-word pill as the app
      header, and the pill REPLACES the battery content while disconnected.

      Visibility is driven in code: this shows only when !connected, and the two
      content rows above hide. The fade between the two states uses the same staged
      RemoteViews-update approach as the icon fade (see AncWidgetProvider.fadeIcons) —
      a home-screen widget has no property animators, so a fade has to be a sequence
      of complete updates with the alpha already baked in.
    -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/widget_conn_row"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:gravity="center"
        android:paddingTop="6dp"
        android:paddingBottom="6dp"
        android:visibility="gone">

        <ImageView
            android:id="@+id/widget_conn_dot"
            android:layout_width="10dp"
            android:layout_height="10dp"
            android:scaleType="fitCenter"
            android:src="@drawable/ic_status_dot_empty"
            android:contentDescription="@string/conn_status_desc" />

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/widget_conn_text"
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginStart="6dp"
            android:text="@string/conn_off"
            android:textColor="@color/widget_text_secondary"
            android:textSize="12sp"
            android:textStyle="bold" />
    </LinearLayout>
</LinearLayout>
